# What the knowledge graph is built from, stated once and visibly.
#
# This replaces `graphify-scope/`, a hand-curated *copy* of the same selection.
# A copy states its exclusions only by being diffed against the live tree, so
# nobody notices when it drifts - and it had: the copy was missing twelve
# documents the audit's own map tiered as required or current, among them the whole
# of Tier 4 ("the traps that would invalidate a conclusion") except TRAPS.md.
# The graph asserted structure over the audit while omitting the documents the
# audit's own map calls most important.
#
# The document rules below follow README.md's "Generated files" section and the
# old DOCUMENT_MAP.md's "Do not read" list (folded into README.md on 2026-09-20).
# When that section changes, change this file with it.

# --- Third-party and generated trees ---------------------------------------
# Also in .gitignore, repeated here so the scan policy survives a .gitignore
# edit: together these hold ~21500 .py files against the ~114 that are ours.
/repos/
/user_data/
# 43 third-party library licences and READMEs, not this project's
# (README.md, "Generated files").
/ftenv/
# Archived by design, including a superseded German regime-definition draft.
/old/
# 896 per-strategy cards; open one only when that strategy is in question.
/corpus/
# Third-party strategy sources with our repairs applied - measured, not read.
/repair/patched/
# The graph's own output, and the copy this file replaces.
/graphify-out/
/graphify-scope/

# --- Documents README.md says not to read -----------------------------
# The five hand-picked case studies of the predecessor work: a case study,
# not a population.
/ANALYSIS.md
/ANALYSIS.ru.md
/results/*.md
# Provenance and publication front matter for the 900-strategy sweep.
/CORPUS.md
/CORPUS_PLAN.md
# Self-contained side investigations with no regime content.
/DCA.md
/DEPTH.md
/RESOLVABLE.md
# Repair provenance; needed only when a repaired implementation is discussed.
/repair/REGISTER.md
/repair/FREQAI_RESULTS.md
/repair/TRANSLATION_AUDIT.md

# --- Agent configuration, not audit content ---------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md

# --- Data and generated output, not machinery -------------------------------
# graphify reads .json as source. 341 of them here are evidence stores and
# result manifests - what the machinery produced, not how it is built. They
# would outnumber the 114 Python modules three to one and say nothing about
# structure. `graphify-out/memory/` is exempt by graphify's own design: past
# query answers are filed back in as corpus.
*.json
*.html
requirements*.txt
